  "note": "reui.io — shadcn-compatible block/component library (1,728 registry items: 1,647 registry:block, 77 registry:ui, 4 hooks). Every page's leaf slug IS the registry name and every parent segment is a fixed category path, so the pattern carries one literal-path template per category (a {author}/{*} parent capture would put the category in front of the id — see tools/sitemap-items.mjs — and produce '<category>-<name>', which matches no registry item). 61 block categories (/blocks/<category>/<sub>/{name}, <sub> optional: /blocks/application/{name} is a listing, not a component) + 72 component categories (/components/<category>/{name}). The 22 /components/<base> and /docs/components/base|radix/<base> pages (alert, stepper, data-grid, …) are already the llms docs urls of the 77 registry:ui items, and a registry item with a url is never overwritten — they attach nothing, so they are not templates. attach_only: pages without a twin make no item (0 new items) — ~380 URLs are newer than the registry snapshot (c-time-picker-1…, chart-31, sheet-12, app-shell-22, pricing-*, compare-*, whiteboard-*) or listings/docs. /icons/*, /template*, /templates/*, /legal/*, /docs/* (except the component docs above), /pricing, /mcp, /alternatives/* stay out. robots.txt disallows /account, /checkout, /login, /blocks/favorites, /api/, /preview/ — no template matches them."
